		<title>boole.sh — Lossless compression for AI</title>
		<meta name="description" content="Zero-loss compression engineered for model weights, tensors, and AI infrastructure. Smaller models. Faster inference. No accuracy lost." />
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
		<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
	</head>
	<body>
		<nav>
			<div class="nav-inner">
				<a href="/" class="logo">boole<span class="accent">.sh</span></a>
				<div class="nav-links">
					<a href="#how">How it works</a>
					<a href="#benchmarks">Benchmarks</a>
					<a href="https://github.com/boole-sh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</nav>

		<main>
			<section class="hero">
				<div class="hero-content">
					<p class="tagline">Lossless compression for AI</p>
					<h1>Shrink models.<br />Keep every bit.</h1>
					<p class="subtitle">
						boole.sh is a zero-loss compression engine purpose-built for model weights,
						activations, and tensor data. We exploit the statistical structure of neural
						network parameters to achieve compression ratios that general-purpose codecs cannot.
					</p>
					<div class="cta-row">
						<a href="https://github.com/boole-sh" class="btn-primary">View source</a>
						<a href="mailto:hello@boole.sh" class="btn-secondary">Get in touch</a>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="hero-visual">
					<div class="compression-demo">
						<div class="demo-bar original">
							<span class="bar-label">Original (FP16)</span>
							<div class="bar-fill" style="width: 100%"></div>
							<span class="bar-value">14.0 GB</span>
						</div>
						<div class="demo-bar zstd">
							<span class="bar-label">zstd -19</span>
							<div class="bar-fill" style="width: 72%"></div>
							<span class="bar-value">10.1 GB</span>
						</div>
						<div class="demo-bar boole">
							<span class="bar-label">boole.sh</span>
							<div class="bar-fill" style="width: 41%"></div>
							<span class="bar-value">5.7 GB</span>
						</div>
						<p class="demo-caption">Llama 3 8B — lossless, bit-exact reconstruction</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="claims">
				<div class="claim">
					<span class="claim-number">2.4x</span>
					<span class="claim-label">median compression ratio on transformer weights</span>
				</div>
				<div class="claim">
					<span class="claim-number">0</span>
					<span class="claim-label">bits of information lost — every weight reconstructs exactly</span>
				</div>
				<div class="claim">
					<span class="claim-number">&gt;2 GB/s</span>
					<span class="claim-label">decompression throughput — no bottleneck at inference time</span>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="how" class="how">
				<h2>Built for how neural networks actually look</h2>
				<p class="section-intro">
					General-purpose compressors treat model files as arbitrary byte streams.
					We don't. boole.sh understands tensor layout, exploits cross-layer correlations,
					and encodes the specific distributions that emerge from gradient descent.
				</p>
				<div class="features">
					<div class="feature">
						<h3>Tensor-aware entropy coding</h3>
						<p>
							Adaptive arithmetic coding tuned to the heavy-tailed distributions
							of trained parameters. Per-channel statistics, not per-file.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature">
						<h3>Format-native ingestion</h3>
						<p>
							Reads SafeTensors, GGUF, PyTorch, and ONNX directly.
							No preprocessing, no conversion step.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature">
						<h3>Streaming decompression</h3>
						<p>
							Layer-by-layer decode directly into GPU memory.
							Load a compressed model as fast as an uncompressed one.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature">
						<h3>Rust + SIMD kernels</h3>
						<p>
							The core engine is ~8k lines of Rust with hand-tuned
							AVX-512 and NEON paths. No runtime dependencies.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="benchmarks" class="benchmarks">
				<h2>Benchmarks</h2>
				<p class="section-intro">
					Compression ratio (higher is better) on popular open-weight models.
					All results are lossless — decompressed output is byte-identical to the original.
				</p>
				<div class="table-wrap">
					<table>
						<thead>
							<tr>
								<th>Model</th>
								<th>Format</th>
								<th>Original</th>
								<th>zstd -19</th>
								<th>boole.sh</th>
								<th>Ratio</th>
							</tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody>
							<tr>
								<td>Llama 3 8B</td>
								<td>FP16</td>
								<td>14.0 GB</td>
								<td>10.1 GB</td>
								<td>5.7 GB</td>
								<td><strong>2.46x</strong></td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td>Mistral 7B</td>
								<td>FP16</td>
								<td>13.5 GB</td>
								<td>9.8 GB</td>
								<td>5.5 GB</td>
								<td><strong>2.45x</strong></td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td>Phi-3 Mini</td>
								<td>FP16</td>
								<td>7.6 GB</td>
								<td>5.6 GB</td>
								<td>3.3 GB</td>
								<td><strong>2.30x</strong></td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td>SDXL (UNet)</td>
								<td>FP16</td>
								<td>5.1 GB</td>
								<td>3.9 GB</td>
								<td>2.3 GB</td>
								<td><strong>2.22x</strong></td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td>Whisper Large v3</td>
								<td>FP32</td>
								<td>6.2 GB</td>
								<td>4.4 GB</td>
								<td>2.4 GB</td>
								<td><strong>2.58x</strong></td>
							</tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="architecture">
				<h2>Architecture</h2>
				<div class="arch-diagram">
					<pre><code>┌─────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐     ┌───────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐
│  Model File │────▶│ Format Parse │────▶│ Tensor Analyze│────▶│ Entropy Code │
│ .safetensors│     │  (engine-    │     │  (engine-     │     │  (engine-    │
│ .gguf .pt   │     │   formats)   │     │   quant)      │     │   core)      │
└─────────────┘     └──────────────┘     └───────────────┘     └──────────────┘
                                                                       │
                    ┌──────────────┐     ┌───────────────┐             │
                    │  .boole file │◀────│ SIMD Kernels  │◀────────────┘
                    │  (compact)   │     │ (engine-      │
                    │              │     │  kernels)     │
                    └──────────────┘     └───────────────┘</code></pre>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="why">
				<h2>Why this matters</h2>
				<div class="why-grid">
					<div class="why-card">
						<h3>Storage costs</h3>
						<p>
							Model registries at scale store thousands of checkpoints.
							2.4x compression directly halves your S3 bill.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="why-card">
						<h3>Distribution</h3>
						<p>
							Smaller artifacts mean faster pulls. Deploy models to edge
							nodes and mobile devices without multi-hour downloads.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="why-card">
						<h3>Cold start</h3>
						<p>
							Streaming decompression lets serverless inference start
							serving requests while the model is still loading.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="bottom-cta">
				<h2>We're building the compression layer for AI infrastructure.</h2>
				<p>If you're working on model serving, distribution, or storage at scale — let's talk.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a href="mailto:hello@boole.sh" class="btn-primary">Contact us</a>
					<a href="https://github.com/boole-sh" class="btn-secondary">GitHub</a>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>

		<footer>
			<p>&copy; 2026 boole.sh</p>
		</footer>
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	:root {
		--bg: #0a0a0b;
		--surface: #141416;
		--border: #2a2a2e;
		--text: #e8e8ec;
		--text-muted: #8a8a94;
		--accent: #6ee7b7;
		--accent-dim: #2d6b54;
		--mono: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
		--sans: 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif;
	}

	* {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		box-sizing: border-box;
	}

	html {
		scroll-behavior: smooth;
	}

	body {
		font-family: var(--sans);
		background: var(--bg);
		color: var(--text);
		line-height: 1.6;
		-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
	}

	nav {
		position: fixed;
		top: 0;
		width: 100%;
		z-index: 100;
		background: rgba(10, 10, 11, 0.85);
		backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.nav-inner {
		max-width: 1200px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 1rem 2rem;
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.logo {
		font-family: var(--mono);
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--text);
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.accent {
		color: var(--accent);
	}

	.nav-links {
		display: flex;
		gap: 2rem;
	}

	.nav-links a {
		color: var(--text-muted);
		text-decoration: none;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		transition: color 0.2s;
	}

	.nav-links a:hover {
		color: var(--text);
	}

	main {
		max-width: 1200px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 0 2rem;
	}

	.hero {
		padding-top: 8rem;
		padding-bottom: 4rem;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 4rem;
		align-items: center;
		min-height: 90vh;
	}

	.tagline {
		font-family: var(--mono);
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		color: var(--accent);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.hero h1 {
		font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: 1.1;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.subtitle {
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		line-height: 1.7;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		max-width: 520px;
	}

	.cta-row {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1rem;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}

	.btn-primary {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
		background: var(--accent);
		color: var(--bg);
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		text-decoration: none;
		border-radius: 6px;
		transition: opacity 0.2s;
	}

	.btn-primary:hover {
		opacity: 0.85;
	}

	.btn-secondary {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		color: var(--text);
		font-weight: 500;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		text-decoration: none;
		border-radius: 6px;
		transition: border-color 0.2s, color 0.2s;
	}

